            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>Basements are some of the most polluted rooms in any home. Limited ventilation, higher humidity, concrete walls that hold moisture, and stored belongings all create conditions where mold spores, dust mites, VOCs from paint and adhesives, and musty odors build up fast. According to the<a href=\"https://www.epa.gov/mold\"> <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">EPA</span></a>, one-third to one-half of all structures have damp conditions that encourage pollutants like mold and bacteria, and basements are often where those conditions are worst.</p><p>An air purifier will not fix a foundation crack or a drainage issue, but a well-matched unit makes a real, measurable difference in the air quality down there. Here are five options sized to different basements and different concerns.</p><h3><strong>The 5 Best Basement Air Purifiers</strong></h3><h4><strong>Pick #1: Blueair Blue Pure 211i Max, Best for Large Basements</strong></h4>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "s3"
          }
        },
        "image_caption_aree8w": {
          "type": "image_caption",
