            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-0",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>For open-plan or full-size basements, the<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/products/blue-pure-211i-max\"> <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Blue Pure 211i Max</span></a> is the strongest option on this list. With a CADR of Pollen 450 cfm, Dust 452 cfm, Smoke 435 cfm, and a recommended coverage of 674 sq ft, the unit cleans a large basement in about 12.5 minutes. HEPASilent™ technology combines mechanical and electrostatic filtration to remove 99.97% of airborne particles down to 0.1 microns, including mold spores, dust, pet dander, and allergens.</p><p>What makes the 211i Max especially useful in a basement is its three built-in sensors (PM1, PM2.5, and PM10). Auto mode reads the air in real time and adjusts fan speed on the fly, so when someone starts a load of laundry or kicks up dust moving storage boxes, the purifier ramps up automatically. Voice control through Alexa and Google Assistant is included, along with full<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/pages/blueair-app\"> <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">app connectivity</span></a> for scheduling and monitoring from upstairs.</p><h3><strong>Pick #2: Blueair Blue Pure 311i+ Max, Best for Mid-Size Basements with Moisture Concerns</strong></h3>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
        "image_caption_673m3j": {
          "type": "image_caption",
          "settings": {
